  "id": "hypochondriasis",
  "term": "hypochondriasis",
  "definition": "Hypochondriasis is a condition marked by persistent worry or belief that one has a serious illness because bodily symptoms are misunderstood. The central feature is preoccupation with feared disease despite the concern being based on misinterpreting physical sensations.",
